            "kind": "link",
            "id": "crate",
            "text": "crates.io/crates/cw-network",
            "url": "http://crates.io/crates/cw-network"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "readme",
            "text": "cw-network models the links between machines and services as a graph with per-link latency and loss. Delivery is ordered by arrival tick then by a stable sequence number, so two runs of the same world deliver the same packets in the same order. Loss is drawn from a seeded stream via hashseed, never from the host."
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "m-h",
            "text": "Modules",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "m-0",
            "text": "cw_network::graph — nodes and links"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "m-1",
            "text": "cw_network::link — a directed edge with latency and loss"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "m-2",
            "text": "cw_network::queue — the in-flight packet queue"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "m-3",
            "text": "cw_network::route — shortest paths by latency"
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "i-h",
            "text": "Items",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "i-0",
            "text": "struct Network — The node and link graph plus the in-flight queue."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "i-1",
            "text": "struct Link — A directed edge with latency_us and loss_per_million."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "i-2",
            "text": "fn deliver — Advances the queue to a tick and returns the packets that arrived, in total order."
