          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "id": "crate",
            "text": "crates.io/crates/detclock",
            "url": "http://crates.io/crates/detclock"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "readme",
            "text": "detclock is a clock for simulations and tests. now() is a tick, advance(n) moves it and fires due timers, and nothing reads the wall clock. Timers with the same due tick fire in the order they were registered, so a run is reproducible. An optional feature provides a tokio-compatible time driver."
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "m-h",
            "text": "Modules",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "m-0",
            "text": "detclock::clock — the logical clock"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "m-1",
            "text": "detclock::timer — scheduled callbacks"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "m-2",
            "text": "detclock::tokio — a tokio time driver (feature)"
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "i-h",
            "text": "Items",
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "i-0",
            "text": "struct Clock — The logical clock; cheap to clone, shared by reference count."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "i-1",
            "text": "struct Timer — A handle to a scheduled callback; dropping it cancels."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "i-2",
            "text": "fn advance — Moves the clock forward and fires every timer due, in order."
          },
