          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "readme",
            "text": "atlas-sim connects to an Atlas server, creates a world from a seed, steps it by ticks and reads any machine's screen, file system or network. Calls are serialised so a run is a function of the seed and the call order. A stub server behind a feature flag runs a world in-process for tests."
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "m-h",
            "text": "Modules",
            "level": 2
          },
