          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "name",
            "text": "Crate replaylog 0.3.0",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "desc",
            "text": "Record every input to a system and replay it later, byte for byte, with a diff of what changed."
          },
          {
            "kind": "styled",
            "id": "use",
            "text": "[dependencies]\nreplaylog = \"0.3.0\"",
            "style": {
              "mono": true,
              "size": 13,
              "padding": 8,
              "background": "#f4f4f4",
              "radius": 4
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "meta",
            "text": "MIT · owner northstar · built with the nightly toolchain on 2026-09-18 for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu · build passing"
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "id": "crate",
            "text": "crates.io/crates/replaylog",
            "url": "http://crates.io/crates/replaylog"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "readme",
            "text": "replaylog writes every input a system receives to an append-only log with its tick, and reads the log back to drive the system again. A replay that diverges reports the first tick at which the output differed and what the difference was. Logs are canonical JSON lines through tinyjson-rs; the diff uses ordmap to keep its report stable."
          },
          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "m-h",
            "text": "Modules",
            "level": 2
          },
